2. SAP PM Core Functional Questions
6) What is SAP Plant Maintenance?
Sample answer:
SAP Plant Maintenance is a module used to manage maintenance activities for technical assets and equipment. It supports equipment master data, functional locations, preventive maintenance, breakdown maintenance, notifications, work orders, task lists, maintenance plans, and reporting. Its main goal is to improve asset reliability, reduce downtime, and support efficient maintenance execution.
7) What are the key master data elements in SAP PM?
Sample answer:
The key master data elements in SAP PM include:
•	Functional Location – represents the place where an asset is installed
•	Equipment Master – represents the individual physical asset
•	Bill of Materials (BOM) – list of spare parts/components
•	Task List – standard sequence of maintenance operations
•	Maintenance Plan – schedule for preventive maintenance
•	Work Center – responsible team or resource group
Accurate master data is critical because poor master data causes reporting issues, work order failures, and planning inefficiencies.
8) What is the difference between Equipment and Functional Location?
Sample answer:
A Functional Location represents the location or system structure where maintenance is managed, while Equipment represents the actual physical asset installed there. Functional locations are more about hierarchy and location structure, while equipment is about individual asset history, maintenance records, and performance tracking. Equipment can be installed at or dismantled from a functional location.
9) What is the difference between preventive maintenance and breakdown maintenance in SAP PM?
Sample answer:
Preventive maintenance is planned and scheduled in advance using maintenance plans and task lists to avoid failures. Breakdown maintenance is reactive and triggered after a failure occurs, usually through notifications and emergency work orders. Preventive maintenance improves reliability and reduces downtime, while breakdown maintenance focuses on restoring operations quickly after failure.
10) What is a maintenance notification?
Sample answer:
A maintenance notification is used to record a problem, malfunction, maintenance request, or breakdown. It captures issue details such as asset, priority, description, damage, cause, and required action. Notifications are often the starting point for maintenance processing and may later lead to creation of a work order.
11) What is a maintenance order in SAP PM?
Sample answer:
A maintenance order is the execution document used to plan, schedule, assign labor, reserve materials, capture costs, and record completion of maintenance work. It is more detailed and actionable than a notification. Orders go through stages like creation, release, execution, technical completion, and settlement.
12) What are common transaction codes used in SAP PM?
Sample answer:
Some commonly used SAP PM transaction codes are:
•	IE01 / IE02 / IE03 – Create/Change/Display Equipment
•	IL01 / IL02 / IL03 – Create/Change/Display Functional Location
•	IW21 / IW22 / IW23 – Create/Change/Display Notification
•	IW31 / IW32 / IW33 – Create/Change/Display Order
•	IW38 / IW39 – Order list and analysis
•	IP01 / IP02 / IP03 – Maintenance Plan
•	IP10 – Maintenance plan scheduling
•	IH01 – Functional location/equipment list
13) How do maintenance plans work in SAP PM?
Sample answer:
Maintenance plans are used to schedule preventive maintenance activities based on time, performance, or strategy. They are linked with task lists and scheduling parameters. When the schedule reaches a due date or counter threshold, the system generates maintenance calls, notifications, or work orders. This helps standardize recurring maintenance and reduce reactive failures.
14) What is a task list?
Sample answer:
A task list is a predefined list of maintenance operations, labor steps, and sometimes components required for a maintenance job. It standardizes execution and ensures consistency across similar activities. In preventive maintenance, task lists are often linked to maintenance plans.
15) How does SAP PM integrate with SAP MM?
Sample answer:
SAP PM integrates with SAP MM mainly for spare parts and procurement. When a maintenance order requires materials, components can be planned and reserved, and procurement can be triggered if stock is unavailable. This ensures maintenance execution is aligned with material availability. Good integration between PM and MM is important to avoid order delays and plant downtime.
