Q13) Users are repeatedly raising the same type of ticket. What would you do?
Sample answer:
If the same ticket is repeating, it means the support team is solving the symptom, not the root cause. I would analyze the ticket pattern, identify the root issue, and then address it through permanent corrective action. This may involve configuration changes, validation rules, SOP updates, dashboards, master data cleanup, or user training. Repeat ticket reduction is one of the most important indicators of mature support.
Q14) You are handling multiple high-priority tickets at once. How will you manage them?
Sample answer:
I would prioritize by business impact, production dependency, SLA deadline, and number of affected users or plants. Then I would assign clear owners within the team, break down tasks, and ensure communication is active for all affected stakeholders. I would focus first on the issue with highest business risk while ensuring the others continue progressing with visibility and control.
