6. SAP PM Deep-Dive Questions Likely at Accenture
Q22) What are the important master data objects in SAP PM?
Sample answer:
The important master data objects are functional location, equipment, BOM, task list, maintenance plan, and work center. These objects are the foundation of maintenance planning, execution, and reporting. In support environments, many recurring issues are caused by poor master data quality, so this area is very important.
Q23) How does SAP PM integrate with MM?
Sample answer:
SAP PM integrates with MM for spare parts planning, reservation, procurement, and inventory support. When work orders require materials, the PM process depends on MM data and availability. Strong PM-MM integration helps ensure timely maintenance execution and reduces delays caused by spare part shortages.
Q24) What is preventive maintenance in SAP PM?
Sample answer:
Preventive maintenance is the planned scheduling of maintenance activities to avoid equipment failure before it happens. In SAP PM, this is managed through maintenance plans, task lists, cycles, and scheduling rules. It is a critical area because it reduces downtime and improves asset reliability.
Q25) What are common causes of SAP PM support issues?
Sample answer:
Common causes include incorrect master data, missing or wrong configuration, authorization issues, process misunderstanding, incomplete integration mapping, and insufficient user training. In many cases, the real issue is a combination of system and process gaps rather than a purely technical defect.
